  (text "Sense resistor\n1 ohm = 1 mV/mA" (at 109.22 132.08 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 054b7dd1-6655-41ba-b68a-5fbc088b8b3c)
  )
  (text "Voltage scaler\nA_{v} = 0.1" (at 48.26 133.35 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 14d720b5-2550-414b-addd-755d6711fed9)
  )
  (text "0.2 V_{pp}" (at 140.97 44.45 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 4488cc01-e541-4100-b370-65b18ea7b5db)
  )
  (text "NOTE: This circuit did not\nperform adequately at high\naudio frequencies, as shown\nin the video."
    (at 222.25 182.88 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 503ff3dd-e57e-4eb3-a1cb-5a992b27853d)
  )
  (text "O'scope ch 2" (at 175.26 96.52 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 5bcfdd79-ce8d-429c-9c9e-a17f5dfb0900)
  )
  (text "Rev B: Add decoupling capacitors C108, C109.\n       Mark C103 'not fitted' - circuit did not oscillate with it absent.\n       Interchange inverting and non-inverting inputs of U102 to make\n       current and voltage outputs have the same sign. \n\nRev. C: Restored C103 - circuit did indeed oscillate under a capacitive load."
    (at 160.02 166.37 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 87f7c0e0-5a9d-4d10-bc85-e5a7eefd621b)
  )
  (text "Split feedback:\nf_{t} = 1/[2π(R_{101} || R_{102})C_{103}]\nf_{t} ≈ 265 kHz"
    (at 35.56 35.56 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 8dea7415-f696-4b79-b771-ad910b36aaf3)
  )
  (text "U101 - TL071 or other JFET-input op amp\nU102 - INA823DR instrumentation amp\nC101, C102 - 25V aluminum electrolytic\nC103-C107 - X7R or Z5V ceramic, >=25 V\nAll resistors 1% metal film"
    (at 19.05 198.12 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 939ad85d-a800-4204-8245-fcf708057f48)
  )
  (text "2 V_{pp}" (at 22.86 24.13 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 93e545e7-fae1-4059-b66e-add33845f127)
  )
  (text "Theory of operation:\n\nConnect AWG to J101 and set to output a 2V_{pp} sine wave at the desired frequency.\nConnect oscilloscope to J103/J104 as indicated.\n\nU101, Q101, Q102 form an amplifier with a gain of 0.1, energizing the speaker\nunder test. (Q101 and Q102 supply a current boost, in case a low-impedance\nspeaker is being tested.) \n\nR104. inside the feedback loop of the amplifier, senses the current \nsupplied to the speaker, at 1 mV/mA. Instrumentation amplifier U102 \namplifies this voltage with a gain of approximately 100, giving\nan output of 0.1 V/mA, or 2.5 V_{pp} at full scale if the speaker's \nimpedance is the nominal 8 ohms.  R105 sets this gain. It may be desirable\nto increase the gain. A 200 ohm resistor at R1 will yield a gain of 500,\nor 6.25 volts full scale for a nominal 8 ohm speaker.\n\nThe signal generator amplitude may be adjusted to give a tolerable volume at\nthe speaker, to optimize the SAF (Spousal Acceptance Factor) of this experiment.\n"
    (at 184.15 54.61 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid b02d3b55-4e46-4536-8edc-e062f6b061f8)
  )
  (text "Current booster" (at 86.36 130.81 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid b9db26f0-b14a-40a9-a4a0-864a1900930a)
  )
  (text "POWER\nSUPPLY" (at 22.86 154.94 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid c777dbeb-6261-4c9a-a273-19c4492c1f66)
  )
  (text "Sense amplifier\nA_{v} = 100\n100 mV/mA" (at 144.78 133.35 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid e8532c47-72e2-4b8c-94a2-248bba9e899f)
  )
  (text "O'scope ch 1" (at 166.37 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid edc566d0-f1f2-47b4-b66e-3bff2f9a18e7)
  )
